  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC phase-out management plan (stage II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to implement the second stage of Uganda&apos;s HCFC Phase-Out Management Plan (HPMP) from June 2024 to May 2027, supporting the country in reducing HCFC consumption by 67.5% by 2025, in compliance with the Montreal Protocol. With a total funding of $138,000 (UNEP: $80 ,000, UNIDO: $58,000), the plan focuses on strengthening enforcement of ozone-depleting substances (ODS) regulations, building capacity for safe handling of low-GWP refrigerants, establishing centers of excellence, and promoting energy efficiency in the refrigeration and air conditioning (RAC) sector. The activities also include awareness programs, stakeholder consultations, and implementing green procurement policies to phase out HCFCs while maintaining energy efficiency.</narrative>
  </description>
